From 41311f50a539d50073f5d54ece90864ce3b004f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:50:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sensorservice: give each app the sensor mode of its profile

The system server writes the mode of every app (folded, raw, invented, none) to
a file; the sensor service reads it at most once per second and applies it in
SensorEventConnection::sendEvents, scratch and no-scratch path, and refuses a
direct channel for the sensors that a mode changes. A file that is missing,
owned by anyone but the system or writable by others leaves every app on the
folded events of the previous change. The headers are host-tested in
privacy/compartments-profiles.
---
 .../sensorservice/SensorDirectConnection.cpp  |  11 +-
 .../sensorservice/SensorEventConnection.cpp   |  28 +--
 services/sensorservice/SensorModeProduction.h |  23 +++
 services/sensorservice/SensorModeSource.h     |  95 ++++++++++
 services/sensorservice/SensorModes.h          | 172 ++++++++++++++++++
 services/sensorservice/SubstituteStream.h     | 140 ++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 454 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 services/sensorservice/SensorModeProduction.h
 create mode 100644 services/sensorservice/SensorModeSource.h
 create mode 100644 services/sensorservice/SensorModes.h
 create mode 100644 services/sensorservice/SubstituteStream.h

